{
  "id": "COMPOUND:29908 - PROTEIN:5802",
  "verbalization": "Aspafilioside C is implicated in the target pathway leading to Hs746T through multiple intermediate molecules, all of which are involved in caspase signaling. The evidence suggests that Aspafilioside C directly targets Caspase-5, which is a key enzyme in the execution of apoptosis. Caspase-5 is subsequently targeted by several structurally diverse compounds, including (2R,3S,4R,5R,6S)-2-[2-(3,4-dihydroxy-5-methoxyphenyl)-7-hydroxy-3-[(2R,3S,4R,5R,6S)-3,4,5-trihydroxy-6-(hydroxymethyl)oxan-2-yl]oxychromenylium-5-yl]oxy-6-(hydroxymethyl)oxane-3,4,5-triol and 2,4-Bis[(4-hydroxyphenyl)methyl]-5-methoxy-3-[2-(3-methoxyphenyl)ethyl]phenol. These compounds all share a common mechanism of action, targeting Caspase-5 and ultimately leading to the activation of Hs746T. The integration of these pathways highlights a potential role for Aspafilioside C in modulating caspase-dependent processes, with Hs746T being a downstream effector in this signaling cascade. The evidence supports a direct or indirect relationship between Aspafilioside C and Hs746T through the Caspase-5 pathway, emphasizing the importance of caspase signaling in the biological effects of the compound.",
